WEBVTT

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.050
The tuning of that lxioran failed.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:11.280
It has no greater abilities than a normal Altan.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:20.860
It looks like even the labs on
Cephon don't always succeed.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:25.860
Five of our comrades died
so we could steal that baby!

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.470
What should we do with him?

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.840
We'll have to dispose of him, obviously.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.380
Kill him?

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:40.370
There's no choice, Dusk.
A defective lxioran is no use to us.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:48.690
I'll raise this child.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.930
You?

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:52.560
Raise a defective lxioran?

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:55.400
I'll do it <i>because</i> he's defective.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:31.690
This feels so good! Baths are the best!

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:34.800
Keep your voice down!
The neighbors will hear you.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.170
It's fine!

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.300
Have you already forgotten your gratitude to me,

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.370
the guy who actually dove
into your memories to save you?

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:45.340
The two issues are unrelated.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:46.980
Sheesh...

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.610
Hey, you just peeked at me!

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:52.010
No I didn't!

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:53.350
Oh, right.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:59.190
I have an interview gig tomorrow,
so keep that in mind, yessiree!

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:07.200
You mean your interviewer is...

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:12.640
Miss Shion Arita, your recent
work is the talk of the town.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:13.670
Do you have any comments?

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:17.370
Er, I don't really know how to comment, nosiree.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.880
Oh come on, you don't want to be
an actress one day, or something?

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.550
Don't you think you'd be good in action movies?

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:25.050
Action, Sir?

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:30.020
I checked your family register.
It's pretty complicated, huh?

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:33.090
Your great-grandmother was
an American living in Hawaii,

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.560
who married your great-grandfather
when he immigrated from Japan.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.890
Their eldest daughter went
to Russia and got married,

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:42.030
and her only son returned to Japan
and married a Japanese girl.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:46.340
Now both of your parents are
supposedly living in Moscow.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:51.840
That's right. That's why my Japanese
is a little funny, yessiree.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:58.210
These days, it's easy to fake
family records if you hire a hacker...

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:02.720
Is that right, Sir? I don't really know.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.060
Lots of real weird things
have happened since I met you.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:11.860
There was that strange light
at Tokyo Bay, for one thing...

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.860
Shion, I've seen you destroy
a building with your fists,

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.230
and jump so high you're practically flying, too.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:22.810
Are you sure you weren't drunk, Mr. Muroto, Sir?

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.910
This is a serious question.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.480
I don't mean to write an
article about it yet, either.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.250
So I'd like you to answer me.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:32.820
Shion, who are you?

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.920
And you came to the wake
at Shinmyou Books too, right?

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.320
What's your relationship to the old man?

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:46.230
I'm a Space Federation inspector.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:49.100
I came to Earth chasing vicious criminals.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.500
Birdy!

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:58.130
I work day and night on that as a side
job to my pinup girl thing, yessiree!

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.510
Are you satisfied now?

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:10.680
How dare that bitch make fun of me?!

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:19.030
Poor thing, it must've
been so tough being all alone.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:22.370
Don't worry, you can live
at our place from now on.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:26.770
There's ocean and mountains nearby.
It's a very relaxed place.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:31.440
My youngest is looking
forward to gaining a big sister!

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:35.510
And you can just leave all
the moving preparations to me.

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:37.500
You don't need to worry about a thing.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:48.690
Hey, do you know where Mr. Shinmyou is?

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:51.680
Hmm? I just saw him over that way.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.380
Be careful! You're as clumsy as ever.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:16.650
Who left an empty can in the hallway, anyway?!

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:19.050
So, what were you saying about Mr. Muroto?

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:23.360
He's sniffing around about me.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.730
He's not a bad guy, but...

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:29.270
He might come around asking you questions, too.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:32.070
It's okay. I'll throw up a smoke screen.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.500
Thanks.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:36.270
"Shoko Kagami"

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:37.260
Shoko?
"Shoko Kagami"

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:38.040
Shoko?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:42.030
Goodbye, Mr. Shinmyou!
Have a nice life with Miss Arita!

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:49.890
Where could she have gone?!

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.390
We're searching the area right now, I promise.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.790
Shoko...

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:58.730
Did she hate the idea of moving
in with her relatives that much?

00:06:58.730 --> 00:06:58.960
"Yuichi & Shoko Kagami"
Did she hate the idea of moving
in with her relatives that much?

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:02.560
That's probably not it. She said
"Have a nice life with Miss Arita," right?
"Yuichi & Shoko Kagami"

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:03.370
That's probably not it. She said
"Have a nice life with Miss Arita," right?

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:05.570
She's got some weird misunderstanding, huh?

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:08.470
So I'm telling you, that's probably the problem...

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:11.710
She wasn't in her apartment, but
it does look like she's been here.

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:13.980
Do you have any idea where she'd go?

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.810
She's a kid, so I doubt she can get too far, but...

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:19.720
Money!

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:20.700
Huh?

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:24.620
A girl on crutches?

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:28.820
Ah, I did see her. She took some money out of the ATM.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:31.260
Do you know which way she went?

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.960
It looked like she was heading for the station.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:35.930
I'm impressed you figured this out!

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:38.330
I've been on Earth longer than you, after all.

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:40.970
The train will be arriving shortly.

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:43.810
Please stay behind the
white line to avoid any danger.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:46.810
Which way should I head?

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:49.440
Lovelorn girls should go north, I guess.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:54.680
Nataru!

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:55.670
Shoko!

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.490
Where?

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.480
Why is she here, too?!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.530
Shoko, where are you going?

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:05.150
Hey, wait!

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.200
Sheesh...

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:12.290
B-Birdy!

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.000
Shoko.

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.640
Help me!

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:30.720
St-Stop that!

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:32.220
Hey, what are you doing?

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:34.620
Well, uh...

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:40.130
Ouch! This lady's being violent!

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:41.660
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:44.530
Wait, you! How dare you do that to a child?!

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:46.200
Maybe we should call the police.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.340
Y-You've got it all wrong!

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:50.530
Birdy!

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:54.210
Where's Shoko?

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:03.550
I let my guard down. I never
figured she'd pull <i>that</i> trick!

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:06.860
More importantly, try to
watch how you act in public!

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:08.190
Jumping over the platform like that...

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.490
If someone took a picture it'd cause a huge fuss!

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:12.030
Who'd do that?

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.860
Mr. Muroto, for example.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.700
Don't you <i>both</i> say that.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:16.900
"Both"?

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:19.740
Um, uh...

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.170
Oh, look, here we are!

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.080
Hmph. I'll never let you catch me!

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.850
Oh, it's Shion Arita!

00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:34.250
She's finally made her CD debut!

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:35.020
"At Last, Her CD Debut!!"

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:36.920
That's a must-buy, huh?

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:38.450
"At Last, Her CD Debut!!"

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:38.920
Must-buy, yessiree!

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:57.810
So that Federation investigator
really wasn't the one after us.

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:00.140
It's too soon to say for sure.

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:05.650
Just who could kill like that,
if not the lxioran inspector?

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:07.150
You're right.

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:12.250
Only someone with extraordinary
physical strength could kill like that.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:17.060
I can't imagine there are
many non-lxiorans who qualify.

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:21.500
But why should we have to
be killed in such a cruel way?

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:25.970
Why does the investigator hate us so much?

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:27.340
Good question.

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:32.610
I guess there'd be no need for
her to kill us so elaborately.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.140
Then who else is there?

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:40.420
Wait, come to think of it, there is another one...

00:10:40.420 --> 00:10:43.790
You're saying there's
another lxioran on this planet?

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:49.290
Yes, I heard about him a long time ago.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.360
What's so funny?

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.990
Nothing; I just remembered
something from the past.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:04.270
Nobody saw anyone who looked like Shoko.

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:07.680
I'll stop on each floor on my way down.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:09.670
Then I'll make my way up.

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:16.150
I just hope she's somewhere in this building...

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:19.320
I don't think she could get very far.

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.360
Well, her legs are injured, true.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.190
There's that, too, but she...

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:33.840
Paging customer Shion Arita.

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:34.840
- Huh?!

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:39.210
- Miss Shion Arita,
Miss Shoko Kagami is waiting for you

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.680
in front of the elevator on the sixth floor.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:45.670
I <i>repeat:</i> Miss Shion Arita...

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:05.000
It's Shiorin in the flesh, for real!

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:08.700
So that girl wasn't a trick!

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:13.110
Oh my god, it's Shion Arita!
Shion Arita the pinup girl is here!

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:20.780
Over there!

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:25.920
You done shopping now?

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:28.590
Thanks, you're really helping me out.

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:29.960
There she is! It's Shiorin!

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:32.090
Autograph please!

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:33.460
What's all the fuss about?

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:36.300
Beats me. Maybe some celebrity showed up.

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:37.530
Yeah right!

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.100
Autograph, please!

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:43.110
Say "yessiree"!

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.110
I bought your CD!

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.580
Take a pic with me so I can email it!

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:49.200
That damn brat...

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:11.470
Serves you right, stupid pinup girl.

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:15.670
Seriously, Shion Arita is here!
Someone emailed me a pic!

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:18.640
I'm telling you, it wasn't Photoshopped!

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:22.310
She's got some nerve, setting <i>me</i> up like that!

00:13:22.310 --> 00:13:24.110
She's just a kid, you know.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:27.120
Who cares?! When someone picks
a fight with me, I take 'em on!

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:29.110
So you're on the same level as her?

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:34.860
Shiorin!

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:37.660
Birdy? Where are you right now?

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:41.650
Well, some stuff happened...
Anyway, did you find Shoko?

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:47.700
There she is!

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:49.690
I'll call you back!

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:57.280
I'm really sorry! I'm in a hurry!

00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:58.850
Hey!

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:01.350
It's not nice to steal people's cabs, lady.

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:03.320
Follow that taxi!

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:06.720
Oh? In that case, you just leave this to me.

00:14:16.300 --> 00:14:19.070
Driver, shake off the taxi behind us!

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:21.240
Bad people are following me!

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:24.470
All right, now's my chance to show my stuff!

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:41.990
Talk about stubborn.

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:45.430
That driver's pretty good.

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:48.400
That driver's something special.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.870
Dang it, I can run faster than this!

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:54.860
"In Service" "Fare"

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:12.960
Bye-bye!

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:14.890
She got me...

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:16.860
Dammit!

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:18.290
What, that was you?!

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:21.130
You got into this business too?!

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:24.970
"In Service" "Fare"

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:26.400
The fare!

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:26.560
"In Service" "Fare"

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:29.100
We'll beat her to the ferry stop.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:33.380
Hey, do you think Shoko is...

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:35.410
Okay, now...

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:39.410
Where to from here?

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.810
I wonder where I should go?

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:15.350
This is the end of the line.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:17.490
Looks like you have a hard time walking.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.480
How about I help you get ashore?

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:25.090
So you're in your first year of junior high, huh?

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:26.960
Aren't I heavy?

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:28.600
It's no problem!

00:16:28.600 --> 00:16:29.930
Shoko!

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:31.670
How?!

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:34.470
You wanted <i>him</i> to come get you, right?

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:39.370
Wh-What are you saying?! Put me down!

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:40.680
Shoko...

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:43.850
Don't touch me! I hate you, Nataru!

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:47.180
Getting all flirty with Shion Arita...

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:48.980
What are you talking about?

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:52.350
I saw you hugging!

00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:53.660
Me?!

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:57.360
You two were hugging in the hospital hallway!

00:16:57.360 --> 00:17:02.830
Oh! She looked like she was going to fall,
so I held her up, that's all.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:05.820
Man, you really jump to conclusions.

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:08.740
Hmph.

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:10.810
Come on, let's go back to the hospital.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:13.240
Your relative is worried about you.

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:17.650
No. I don't want to go to his stupid house.

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:19.050
Shoko?

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:31.190
I... I...

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:32.590
Shoko?

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:40.070
I don't want to leave you, Nataru.

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:44.900
I can't be with you forever, Shoko.

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:51.410
Your relative seems nice, doesn't he? It'll be okay.

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:05.390
Okay, then, I'll be going.
Miss Arita will be here soon.

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:09.730
You're the boy who came to the
refugee camp to do interviews, right?

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:11.270
Do you know Miss Arita?

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:15.260
Sort of. My name's Tsutomu Senkawa. Bye, then.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:21.880
She likes you a lot, huh Nataru?

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:26.980
We're like siblings. I've known
her since she was tiny, after all.

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:31.050
Hey, what was Shoko's big brother like?

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:32.890
He was a good guy.

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:36.060
He was a good cook and stuff, even
though he didn't look like the type.

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:40.130
Their parents died in an accident,
but he was still always cheerful.

00:18:40.130 --> 00:18:43.770
He was really attached to Shoko.

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:46.670
He sounds like a kind person.

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:49.000
Yeah.

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.510
We used to skip class together.

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:53.840
You shouldn't do that!

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:55.280
Well, true.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:59.980
Come to think of it, the first time I met Kagami,

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:02.580
there was this crazy-loud
noise at the school pond...

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.190
So we slipped out of class to check it out.

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:08.990
That was what started it all.

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:12.930
If he were still alive, I
would've wanted him to meet you.

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:15.330
I'm sure you would've hit it off.

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:25.540
Let's decide on whether you'll move in with us

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:29.850
after you've taken time to heal up your legs here.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:34.020
I'm sorry, I got carried away
and didn't think of your feelings.

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:38.120
Don't hate me, okay?

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:39.520
Thank you.

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:44.160
Looks like things will go well for Shoko.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:46.360
Yeah, she's a cheerful, good girl by nature,

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:48.400
so I'm sure they'll take good care of her.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:54.200
Nataru... are you sure you don't feel lonely?

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:57.040
Don't tease me.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:19:59.340
So I was right!

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:01.340
Hey, you're going to trip again.

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:03.250
I'm fine!

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:04.180
See?

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:05.370
Hey...

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:18.390
Sheesh, you're so clumsy for an lxioran.

00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:21.700
Nataru, you grew taller than me!

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.870
I've been taller than you since we were kids.

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:25.030
Are you sure?

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:26.570
Yes!

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:29.600
Hmm... This feels weird, somehow.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:31.600
You say some strange things.

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:38.370
The Shinmyou Books kid and Shion Arita, eh?

00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:52.930
Mr. Shinmyou...

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:53.860
Yes?

00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:57.130
Starting next week, recycling
pickup will be on Mondays.

00:20:57.130 --> 00:20:58.730
Don't get confused, okay?

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:00.740
Sure, the nonburnable trash is Tuesdays,

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:03.200
and the burnable trash is
Wednesdays and Fridays, right?

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:08.210
It would sure help me if everyone
were as on top of things as you.

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:10.200
Well, if you'll excuse me...

00:23:11.900 --> 00:23:17.010
<i>Nataru was shot by Moss, who</i>
<i>ambushed him in his apartment.</i>

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:22.080
<i>However, as his consciousness dims,</i>
<i>a new power kicks in.</i>

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:24.070
<i>That power</i> is...

00:23:25.350 --> 00:23:30.750
<i>And Birdy receives word from Nataru,</i>
<i>but his words make her uneasy.</i>

00:23:32.450 --> 00:23:36.080
<i>Nataru, what is it you're trying to do?</i>
